## SHACL enforcement

Each example prints a `--json` receipt, and the tracked copy lives in `evidence/examples/`. Every
receipt is a JSON entity, and its example contract declares a SHACL shape that closes it. The
receipt must carry exactly the fields the shape names, with the types and values it allows.
`pv lint contracts/ --gate shapes` checks all of them.

The gate **fails closed**:

- A violation is exit 1.
- pv declines (exit 2) when it cannot measure. For example, a planted control that does not fire
  is a decline, never a pass. pv plants its own broken receipt, and every extractor has a
  planted control. Each of those controls must fire before a pass counts.
- Every shape is armed, and armed shapes only ratchet up against `origin/main`.

<!-- Generated by scripts/readme_sync.sh from pv lint --gate shapes. Do not edit by hand. -->
<!-- SHACL_SUMMARY_START -->
<!-- SHACL_SUMMARY_END -->

Run it locally:

```bash
pv lint contracts/ --gate shapes          # the SHACL gate alone
bash scripts/contracts_gate.sh            # all six steps, the same as CI
```

## Proof status

`contracts/proof-status.json` is the committed proof receipt: the output of
`pv proof-status contracts --binding contracts/binding.yaml --verify-bindings . --format json`,
minus its timestamp. The gate regenerates the receipt and fails if the regenerated copy differs
from the committed one. `scripts/proof_ratchet.sh` fails the gate if any contract's level drops
below `contracts/proof-baseline.json`, if the verified binding count falls, or if more declared Kani
harnesses go missing. The missing harnesses are tracked in
[#6](https://github.com/paiml/rust-mdipierro-nlib/issues/6), and pv's credit for them in
[aprender#4531](https://github.com/paiml/aprender/issues/4531).

